  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development and sharing of knowledge to meet water challenges in the Maghreb</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Maghreb region, water security is threatened under the combined effect of water scarcity, dictated by an unfavourable natural context, human activities and climate change which, in addition, tends to accentuate the frequency and the intensity of extreme events: droughts and floods. In accordance with its IHP 9 program, UNESCO will contribute through the actions that will be implemented by the Rabat Office to the development and sharing of new knowledge on water management systems, the strengthening of capacities of water stakeholders and adaptation of water policies in the Maghreb countries to meet local and global water challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
